    "body": "## Description\n\nImprove `docs/getting-started.md` by adding installation and build instructions for macOS and Windows (via WSL2). The current guide covers Ubuntu/Debian only.\n\n## Steps to Complete\n\n1. Open `docs/getting-started.md`.\n2. Add a section for **macOS** covering:\n   - Installing Homebrew (if not already installed)\n   - Installing dependencies via Homebrew (`cmake`, `ninja`, `pkg-config`, `gtkmm4`, `curl`)\n   - Any macOS-specific notes for GTK 4\n3. Add a section for **Windows (WSL2)** covering:\n   - Installing WSL2 and Ubuntu\n   - Following the existing Ubuntu instructions inside WSL2\n   - A note about GUI support in WSL2 (`wslg`)\n4. Test the commands if you have access to the relevant operating system. If not, note that they are untested and someone with that OS should verify them.\n5. Commit with `docs: add macOS and Windows instructions to getting-started`.\n6. Open a pull request.\n\n## Learning Outcomes\n\n- Writing cross-platform installation documentation.\n- Understanding how GTK 4 dependencies differ across platforms.\n\n## Helpful Resources\n\n- [GTK installation on macOS](https://www.gtk.org/docs/installations/macos/)\n- [WSL2 GUI support (WSLg)](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/wsl/tutorials/gui-apps)\n- [gtkmm installation guide](https://gtkmm.org/en/download.html)\n",
